import hashlib
from pathlib import Path

O = Path('artifacts/paper_evidence/review_round4/protein_depth')
O.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
(O / 'runtime').mkdir(exist_ok=True)
path = O / 'hypothesis.md'
content = "# Hypothesis fixed before depth-correction scoring\n\nThe standard-depth selector score is the probability the trained selector assigns to a candidate when its cell is moved to a reference depth. Every count-scale teacher proposal is multiplied by L_ref/L_c, and the log library-size feature is set to log(1+L_ref). L_ref is the median library size of the training cells. Library size is the sum of the corrupted/input counts in the frozen gene panel, matching the selector feature. Gene mean and dropout features are unchanged. No model is refitted unless its saved fitted model is missing; any necessary exact reconstruction will be disclosed and checked against saved original scores before correction scoring.\n\nPrediction: this removes the depth component, matches or exceeds MAGIC and scVI across the Hao pairs with at least 200 detected training cells, and stays ahead of every comparison in Papalexi on pooled, within-target, and depth-adjusted correlations. Both successes and failures will be reported. No other new variants or tuning are allowed.\n\nThe single secondary ranking is the original selector logit after ordinary least-squares residualization on an intercept and log library size within each gene, followed by ranking the residuals. This regression uses the evaluation candidates for that gene, uses no protein outcomes, and is fixed before bootstrap resampling. If saved probabilities saturate, use reconstructed model logits where available; disclose any clipping otherwise.\n\nEvaluate the unchanged 41 Hao pairs and CD274 in the 3,400-cell and full Papalexi benchmarks. Reuse saved per-cell scores, splits, teacher proposals and fitted models. Retain previously evaluated fused-value variants as comparators, without creating new variants.\n\nUse 2,000 paired bootstrap draws and seed 1729. Hao resamples cells within donor exactly as the original evaluator. Papalexi resamples perturbation targets with the original evaluator's seed tuple derived from 1729. Depth adjustment is the Pearson correlation of ranking and protein rank residuals after regression on ranked log library size plus intercept, recomputed per draw. Within Hao cell types, use the cell-count-weighted mean of defined correlations among types with at least 50 original eligible cells; retain these eligible types during resampling. Papalexi uses its existing within-target definition (at least three cells). Report raw CLR variance explained by categorical group (one-way R-squared), and depth-protein association within Hao level-1 and level-2 types.\n\nAcross-pair summaries include all pairs, <200 and >=200 detected training cells, depth-protein rho below -0.1, between -0.1 and 0.1 inclusive, and above 0.1, plus crossed strata. Pair-bootstrap percentile intervals and exact two-sided sign tests are descriptive because antibody pairs share genes and cell populations. Undefined correlations remain undefined, including library-size partial correlation adjusting for itself.\n"
if path.exists():
    assert path.read_text() == content
else:
    path.write_text(content)
(O / 'runtime/hypothesis.sha256').write_text(hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest() + '\n')
